# Build context = the whole tree (compose: build: .), so this file is what
# `COPY . .` will NOT copy into dzmm-bot:latest.
#
# 2026-09-27 audit (P0): without this file the built image contained
#   .env, .env.bak-*, .dzmm_token.json, .dzmm_token.json.bak-*,
#   profiles.json (666 KB of member PII), state.json
# i.e. platform credentials plus personal data of every archived member,
# sitting inside an image layer. Everything credential- or PII-shaped is
# excluded below, and the deploy gate now refuses to ship without this file.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root; a leading
# "/" pins a pattern to the top level (that is how prompts/*.md stays in while
# root-level notes go out).

# ---- credentials & session ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.dzmm_token.json
.dzmm_token.json.*
.dzmm_login.json
.dzmm_login*.json
token.emergency
bot.paused
.session.lock
.session_version.json
secrets/
/b/
/c/

# ---- runtime state and PII ------------------------------------------------
state.json
profiles.json
profile_scan.json
check_health_state.json
renew_fail_state.json
renew_emergency_state.json
data/
novels/
logs/
pw_profile*/
*.log

# ---- source-only trees (not needed at runtime) ----------------------------
tests/
tools/
docs/
probe/
deploy/
.pylibs/
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.github/

# ---- build / backup artifacts and junk ------------------------------------
*.tar.gz
backup-*
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak[0-9]
*.bak[0-9][0-9]
profiles.json.*
state.json.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
_tmp/
tmp*/
releases/
._*
# Junk left behind by a mistyped curl ("%{http_code}n", a 0-byte file) --
# seen in the build context on 2026-09-27.
%*
# Root-only one-off dev scripts (production modules never start with "_")
/_*.py
# Host-side ops files (Caddy/systemd/scripts) -- they belong on the host, not
# inside the bot image. entrypoint.sh is required and is NOT matched here.
Caddyfile
backup.sh
resume.sh
*.service
/config/config_backups/
docker-compose*.yml
deploy.ps1
/deploy_gate.py
/*.md
